As part of "init unification", the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __moveinit__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __copyinit__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  methods {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/modular/modular/blob/main/mojo/proposals/remove_move_and_copy_init.md"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul are now renamed}} to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 fn __init__(out self, *, take: Self)
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 fn __init__(out self, *, copy: Self)
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  respectively. Mojo now accepts these names for initializers, but also supports the legacy 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __moveinit__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __copyinit__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  names as well (for now). However, the argument name for these legacy methods must now be named 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 take
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 copy
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  respectively. Please move to the more modern 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __init__
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  names when possible.\
