\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 struct
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  type that opts-in to being explicitly destroyed.\uc0\u8232 Libraries with generic algorithms and types should be written to accommodate linear types. Making 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ImplicitlyDestructible
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  opt-in for traits encourages a default stance of support, with specific types and functions only opting-in to the narrower 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ImplicitlyDestructible
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  requirement if they truly need it.\uc0\u8232 The majority of generic algorithms that take their inputs by reference should not be affected.\
