\fs40 \cf2 Collections and iterators\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Dict
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  internals have been replaced with a Swiss Table implementation using SIMD group probing for lookups. This improves lookup, insertion, and deletion performance\'97especially when looking up keys not in the dict\'97while increasing the load factor from 2/3 to 7/8 for better memory efficiency. The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 power_of_two_initial_capacity
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  keyword argument has been renamed to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 capacity
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and now accepts any positive integer (it is rounded up to the next power of two internally, minimum 16).\
\ls12\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Dict
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  now performs in-place tombstone rehashing when the table is full of tombstones but the live element count is low. This prevents unnecessary capacity doubling after repeated insert/delete cycles.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/utils/static_tuple/StaticTuple/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul StaticTuple}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 now supports comparison operators. 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __eq__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 /
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __ne__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  are available when 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 element_type: Equatable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __lt__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 /
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __le__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 /
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __gt__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 / 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __ge__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  are available when 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 element_type: Comparable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . All use lexicographic ordering with compile-time unrolled loops.\
\ls12\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/set/Set/#pop"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul Set.pop()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 now uses {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/dict/Dict/#popitem"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul Dict.popitem()}} directly, avoiding a redundant rehash. Order changes from FIFO to LIFO, matching Python's unordered 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 set.pop()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Set.__gt__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
