\fs40 \cf2 String and text\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Stringable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Representable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  traits are now deprecated. Use 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Writable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  instead to make your types formattable as strings. 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Writable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  provides a default implementation, so in many cases simply adding 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Writable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  conformance is enough without manually implementing 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 write_to()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  or 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 write_repr_to()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , however, you can manually implement these to get custom output.\
\ls13\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 stdlib
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  is beginning to remove support for the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Stringable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Representable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  traits in favor of the unified 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Writable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  trait. Most stdlib types have had their conformance to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Stringable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Representable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  removed and the associated 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __str__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __repr__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  methods have been deprecated.\
\ls13\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __reversed__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  method on 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 String
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/string/string_slice/StringSlice/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul StringSlice}}, and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 StringLiteral
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  has been deprecated in favor of the new 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 codepoints_reversed()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  method. The new method name makes it explicit that iteration is over Unicode codepoints in reverse order, maintaining consistency with the existing 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 codepoints()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 codepoint_slices()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  methods. The deprecated 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __reversed__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  methods will continue to work but will emit deprecation warnings.\
\ls13\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 StringSlice
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  constructor from 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 String
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  now propagates mutability. If you have a mutable reference to a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 String
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 StringSlice(str)
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  returns a mutable 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 StringSlice
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/string/string/String/#as_string_slice"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul String.as_string_slice()}} method is now deprecated in favor of the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 StringSlice(str)
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  constructor, and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 String.as_string_slice_mut()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  has been removed.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/string/string/String/#ljust"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul String.ljust()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
, 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 String.rjust()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and 
