\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul UnsafeUnion}}
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 [*Ts]
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , a C-style untagged union type for FFI interoperability. Unlike 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Variant
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 UnsafeUnion
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  does not track which type is stored (no discriminant), making it suitable for interfacing with C unions and low-level type punning. The memory layout exactly matches C unions (size is max of elements, alignment is max of elements).\uc0\u8232 All element types must have trivial copy, move, and destroy operations, matching C union semantics where types don't have constructors or destructors.\u8232 Construction is explicit (no implicit conversion) to emphasize the unsafe nature of this type. All accessor methods are prefixed with 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 unsafe_
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  to make it clear that these operations are unsafe.\uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb13 from\cf14  ffi \cf5 import\cf14  UnsafeUnion\cb1 \
