\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 .mojo
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  for all Mojo source files and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __init__.mojo
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  for package initialization files. The emoji extensions were removed to simplify the tooling and improve compatibility across different systems and editors.\
\ls22\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 owned
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  keyword has been removed. Use 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 var
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  for parameters or 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 deinit
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  for 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __moveinit__
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 /
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __del__
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  arguments as appropriate.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls22\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Dict.EMPTY
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Dict.REMOVED
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  comptime aliases have been removed. These were internal implementation details of the old hash table design.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls22\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 @nonmaterializable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  decorator has been renamed to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 @__nonmaterializable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . This decorator should not be used outside the standard library, and might be removed in a future release.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs48 \cf2 \uc0\u55357 \u57056 \u65039 
\f0  Fixed\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls23\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Fixed a bug where Mojo incorrectly passed or returned structs in 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 extern
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  C function calls. The compiler now applies platform ABI coercion (System V AMD64 on x86-64, AAPCS on ARM64) when lowering external calls, decomposing structs into the register types the C ABI requires\'97matching the behavior of Clang and Rust. This resolves silent wrong-answer bugs when calling C functions that take or return struct types.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls23\ilvl0\cf5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/modular/modular/issues/5845"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul Issue #5845}}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: Functions raising custom type with conversion fails when returning StringSlice\
\ls23\ilvl0\cf5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/modular/modular/issues/5722"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul Issue #5722}}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __del__
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  incorrectly runs when 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __init__
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  raises before all fields are initialized.\
\ls23\ilvl0\cf5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/modular/modular/issues/5875"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul Issue #5875}}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: Storing 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 SIMD[DType.bool, N]
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  with width > 1 to a pointer and reading back element-wise now returns correct values.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
