Mojo now supports a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/builtin/type_aliases/#never"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul Never}} type, which can never be instantiated. This type can be used for functions (like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/os/os/abort/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul abort()}}) which do not have a normal return value, and for functions that are guaranteed to raise without returning a normal value. Functions that are declared to raise 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Never
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  (and generic functions instantiated with 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Never
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  as their error type) compile into the same ABI as functions that don't 
