The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/builtin/simd/#uint"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul UInt}} struct has been replaced by a new 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 UInt
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  type alias to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Scalar[DType.uint]
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . This is a major change that enables more powerful generic programming by abstracting over unsigned SIMD data dtypes of machine word size.\uc0\u8232 This change will likely break code that relies on implicit conversions to/from 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 UInt
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Int
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 /
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 SIMD
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 SIMD
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  type is also slightly less foldable at compile time, which can cause some code in where clauses, comptime expressions, and other code in parametric contexts to now fail or crash. These shortcomings will be addressed in subsequent patches as needed.\
\ls39\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
