\ls40\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Mojo compiler now supports the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 -Werror
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  flag, which treats all warnings as compilation errors. This is useful for enforcing stricter code quality standards, particularly in CI/CD pipelines. The flag works with the Mojo compiler tools (
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo run
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo build
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo package
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo doc
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ). When used with 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --disable-warnings
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , warnings are promoted to errors first, so the errors are not suppressed.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls40\ilvl1\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The counterpart 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 -Wno-error
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  flag disables treating warnings as errors. When both flags are specified, the last one wins.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls40\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Specifying CUDA architectures with 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --target-accelerator
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  now expects a sm version string rather than just a compute capability. For example, 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --target-accelerator=nvidia:80
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  should be changed to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --target-accelerator=nvidia:sm_80
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . If an incorrect format is used for the version, the compiler will default to the lowest supported sm version.\
\ls40\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Mojo LSP server now debounces document updates to reduce CPU usage during rapid typing. Previously, every keystroke triggered a full document parse; now updates are coalesced with a 150ms delay, reducing parse frequency by 10-50x during active editing.\
\ls40\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Mojo compiler now "diffs" very long types in error messages to explain what is going on in an easier to understand way.\
\ls40\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Elaboration error printing with different levels of verbosity offers control on how parameter values are displayed as part of elaboration errors when function instantiation fails. 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --elaboration-error-verbose=value
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  now takes a value, where:\
