\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
no-params
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  means don't display any concrete parameter values. This is helpful to collapse recursion-related error messages into shorter blobs.\
\ls40\ilvl1
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
simple-params
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  means display concretized parameter values for simple types, including numeric types and strings, in a user-friendly format (default value).\
