\f2\fs48 \cf2 \uc0\u10024 
\f0  Highlights\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls44\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A new, improved {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/memory/unsafe_pointer/UnsafePointer/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul UnsafePointer}} type has been added, and the old version renamed to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 LegacyUnsafePointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . The new version fixes several issues with the old 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 LegacyUnsafePointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls44\ilvl1
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
LegacyUnsafePointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  had constructors that allowed unsafe implicit mutability and origin casts, making it easy to make unsafe changes by accident. The new 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 UnsafePointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  eliminates these.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls44\ilvl1\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The new 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 UnsafePointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  now has an inferred mutability parameter, simplifying the API.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls44\ilvl1
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
UnsafePointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  does not have a default value for its origin parameter, so it must be explicitly specified or unbound. 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 LegacyUnsafePointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  defaults to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 MutAnyOrigin
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , which results in the lifetimes of many values being extended needlessly.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls44\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For more information, see \cf5 \ul Pointer and memory changes\cf2 \ulnone .\
\ls44\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Many enhancements to compile-time errors, including suppressing extraneous messages and preserving more human-readable display for many aliases and parameters. For details, see \cf5 \ul Tooling changes\cf2 \ulnone .\
\ls44\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Added a new document on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/gpu/block-and-warp/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul GPU block and warp operations and synchronization}}.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Language enhancements\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls45\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Mojo now supports the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 comptime
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  keyword as a synonym for 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 alias
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 comptime
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  keyword can be used interchangeably with 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 alias
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  for compile-time declarations. Both keywords are fully supported and produce identical behavior. For example:\uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb13 comptime\cf14  x \cf5 =\cf14  \cf18 5\cf14       \cf6 # New preferred syntax\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls45\ilvl0\cf5 \cb13 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
alias\cf14  y \cf5 =\cf14  \cf18 10\cf14         \cf6 # Still fully supported\cf14 \cb1 \
\ls45\ilvl0\cf5 \cb13 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
comptime\cf14  MyType\cf5 [\cf14 T\cf5 :\cf14  AnyType\cf5 ]\cf14  \cf5 =\cf14  T  \cf6 # Works with parametric declarations\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls45\ilvl0\cf10 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\uc0\u8232 \cf14 \cb13 \uc0\u8232 
\fs32 \cf16 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cf17 \uc0\u8232 \cf16 \uc0\u8232 \cf14 \uc0\u8232 \cb13 \uc0\u8232 \cf2 \cb1 Note: Future updates will migrate error messages and internal terminology to use "comptime". The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 alias
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  keyword will remain supported for backward compatibility for now.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls45\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Mojo now supports unpacking an alias/comptime tuple with a single statement when it is not inside a struct or trait. For example:\uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb13 comptime\cf14  i\cf5 ,\cf14  f \cf5 =\cf14  \cf5 (\cf18 1\cf5 ,\cf14  \cf18 3.0\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls45\ilvl0\cf5 \cb13 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
comptime\cf14  q\cf5 ,\cf14  v \cf5 =\cf14  \cf15 divmod\cf5 (\cf18 4\cf5 ,\cf14  \cf18 5\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls45\ilvl0\cf10 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\uc0\u8232 \cf14 \cb13 \uc0\u8232 
\fs32 \cf16 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cf17 \uc0\u8232 \cf16 \uc0\u8232 \cf14 \uc0\u8232 \cf2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls45\ilvl0\cf5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/modular/modular/issues/3925"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul Issue #3925}}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
