\ls51\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/sync/sync/syncwarp/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul gpu.sync.syncwarp()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 now supports Apple GPUs via 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 SIMDGROUP
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  barrier implementation. On Apple GPUs, this provides execution synchronization for all active lanes using a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 SIMDGROUP
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  barrier with no memory fence. For threadgroup memory ordering, use {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/sync/sync/barrier/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul barrier()}} instead. Note that lane masks are not supported on Apple GPUs, so the mask argument is ignored.\
\ls51\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/primitives/warp/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul gpu.primitives.warp}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 now supports Apple GPUs with native SIMD-group shuffle operations. This enables 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 shuffle_idx()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 shuffle_up()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 shuffle_down()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 shuffle_xor()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  on Apple hardware by mapping Metal 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 simd_shuffle*
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  intrinsics to AIR (
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 llvm.air.simd_shuffle[_up/_down/_xor]
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ) instructions, achieving feature parity with NVIDIA and AMD backends.\
\ls51\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/intrinsics/store_release/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul gpu.intrinsics.store_release()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/intrinsics/load_acquire/"}}{\fldrslt 
