\fs40 \cf2 Performance optimizations\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls54\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Optimized float-to-string formatting performance by eliminating unnecessary stack allocations. Internal lookup tables used for float formatting (
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 cache_f32
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 cache_f64
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ) are now stored as global constants instead of being materialized on the stack for each conversion. This reduces stack overhead by ~10KB for 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float64
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and ~600 bytes for 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float32
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  operations, improving performance for all float formatting operations including 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 print()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , string interpolation, and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 str()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  conversions.\
\ls54\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Optimized number parsing performance by eliminating stack allocations for large lookup tables. Internal lookup tables used for number parsing (
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 powers_of_5_table
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 POWERS_OF_10
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ) are now stored as global constants using the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/builtin/globals/global_constant/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul global_constant}} function instead of being materialized on the stack for each parsing operation. This reduces stack overhead by ~10.6KB for number parsing operations, improving performance for string-to-number conversions including 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 atof()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and related float parsing operations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs40 \cf2 Other library changes\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls55\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/hashlib/hasher/Hasher/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul Hasher}} trait's 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 _update_with_bytes()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  method now takes 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Span[Byte]
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  instead of 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 UnsafePointer[UInt8]
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and a separate length parameter. This change applies to all hasher implementations including 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 AHasher
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Fnv1a
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\ls55\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Philox random number generator (
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Random
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 NormalRandom
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ) has been moved from 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 gpu.random
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/random/philox/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul random.philox}}. These types now work on both CPU and GPU. Import them using 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 from random import Random, NormalRandom
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  or 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 from random.philox import Random, NormalRandom
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

