\ls59\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The way copying is modeled in Mojo has been overhauled. The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Copyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  trait has been updated to represent a type that can be explicitly copied (using a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 copy()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  method), and a new 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ImplicitlyCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  "marker" trait can be used to opt-in to making a type implicitly copyable as well. This swaps the default behavior from being implicitly copyable to being only explicitly copyable. Several standard library traits, types, and functions now require now require explicit 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Copyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  instead of 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ImplicitlyCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . See \cf5 \ul Standard library changes\cf2 \ulnone  for more information.\
\ls59\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
