\fs40 \cf2 Copyability changes\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls62\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The way copying is modeled in Mojo has been overhauled.\uc0\u8232 Previously, Mojo had two traits for modeling copyability:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls62\ilvl1
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Copyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  denoted a type that could be copied implicitly\
\ls62\ilvl1
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
ExplicitlyCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  denoted a type that could only be copied with an explicit call to a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 .copy()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  method.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls62\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The vast majority of types defaulted to implementing 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Copyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  (and therefore were implicitly copyable), and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ExplicitlyCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  was partially phased in but had significant usage limitations.\uc0\u8232 Now, the new 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Copyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  trait instead represents a type that can be explicitly copied (using 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 .copy()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ), and a new 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ImplicitlyCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  "marker" trait can be used to opt-in to making a type implicitly copyable as well. This swaps the default behavior from being implicitly copyable to being only explicitly copyable.\uc0\u8232 The new 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ImplicitlyCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  trait inherits from 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Copyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and requires no additional methods. 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ImplicitlyCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  is known specially to the compiler. (
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ImplicitlyCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  types may also be copied explicitly using 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 .copy()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .)\uc0\u8232 This makes it possible for non-implicitly-copyable types to be used with all standard library functionality, resolving a long-standing issue with Mojo effectively forcing implicit copyability upon all types. This will enable Mojo programs to be more efficient and readable, with fewer performance and correctness issues caused by accidental implicit copies.\u8232 With this change, types that conform to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Copyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  are no longer implicitly copyable:\uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb13 @fieldwise_init\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls62\ilvl0\cf5 \cb13 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
struct\cf14  \cf15 Person\cf5 (\cf14 Copyable\cf5 ):\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls62\ilvl0\cf14 \cb13 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
    \cf5 var\cf14  name\cf5 :\cf14  String\cb1 \
