Mojo is now available independently as the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  Conda package. In includes the Mojo compiler, standard library, and the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 layout
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  package (which is heavily used in GPU programming). It also includes the Mojo developer tools: LSP, debugger, formatter, and so on.\uc0\u8232 To use Python to Mojo interoperability in v25.5, you must install the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 modular
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  package. This will move to the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  package in a future release.\uc0\u8232 For more details, see the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/install/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul install guide}}.\
