The compiler now detects attempts to materialize references to compile-time interpreter stack memory into runtime code. This includes related types that reference memory, like slices, spans, and pointers.\uc0\u8232 The compiler cannot currently track the lifetime of internal stack objects when materialized to runtime, which could cause memory leaks. Consider this example:\u8232 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb13 fn\cf14  \cf15 test_comptime_materialize\cf5 ():\cf14 \cb1 \
