\f2\fs48 \cf2 \uc0\u10024 
\f0  Highlights\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls97\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Check out the new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/gpu/fundamentals/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul GPU basics}} section of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul Mojo Manual}} and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/gpu/intro-tutorial/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul Get started with GPU programming with Mojo and the MAX Driver}} tutorial for a guide to getting started with GPU programming in Mojo!\
\ls97\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Some APIs in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul gpu}} package were enhanced to simplify working with GPUs.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls97\ilvl1\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
If you're executing a GPU kernel only once, you can now skip compiling it first before enqueueing it, and pass it directly to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/host/device_context/DeviceContext/#enqueue_function"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul DeviceContext.enqueue_function()}}.\
\ls97\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The three separate methods on 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 DeviceContext
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  for asynchronously copying buffers between host and GPU memory have been combined to single overloaded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/host/device_context/DeviceContext/#enqueue_copy"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul enqueue_copy()}} method, and the three separate methods for synchronous copies have been combined into an overloaded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/host/device_context/DeviceContext/#copy_sync"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul copy_sync()}} method.\
\ls97\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 gpu.shuffle
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  module has been renamed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/primitives/warp/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul gpu.warp}} to better reflect its purpose.\
\ls97\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul gpu}} package API documentation has been expanded, and API documentation for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/kernels/layout/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul layout}} package is underway, beginning with core types, functions, and traits.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls97\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
See the \cf5 \ul Standard library changes\cf2 \ulnone  section of the changelog for more information.\
\ls97\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The legacy 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 borrowed
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 /
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 inout
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  keywords and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 -> T as foo
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  syntax are no longer supported and now generate a compiler error. Please move to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 read
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 /
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mut
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 /
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 out
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  argument syntax instead. See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/values/ownership/#argument-conventions"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul Argument conventions}} in the Mojo Manual for more information.\
\ls97\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The standard library has many changes related to strings. Notably, the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Char
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  type has been renamed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/string/codepoint/Codepoint/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul Codepoint}}, to better capture its intended purpose of storing a single Unicode codepoint. Additionally, related method and type names have been updated as well. See \cf5 \ul Standard library changes\cf2 \ulnone  for more details.\
\ls97\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Support has been added for 128- and 256-bit signed and unsigned integers. This includes the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/builtin/dtype/DType/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul DType}} aliases 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 DType.int128
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 DType.uint128
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 DType.int256
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 DType.uint256
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/builtin/simd/SIMD/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul SIMD}} support for 128- and 256-bit signed and unsigned element types. Note that this exposes capabilities (and limitations) of LLVM, which may not always provide high performance for these types and may have missing operations like divide, remainder, etc. See \cf5 \ul Standard library changes\cf2 \ulnone  for more details.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

