\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 String()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  constructors instead. See \cf5 \ul Standard library changes\cf2 \ulnone  for more details.\
\ls104\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The standard library has many changes related to strings. The new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/string/codepoint/Codepoint/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul Char}} struct represents a single Unicode character, and includes several methods for categorizing character types. When iterating over the characters of a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 String
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  with a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 for
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  loop, you now should use the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/string/string/String/#chars"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul String.chars()}} method to provide an iterator of 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Char
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values or the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/string/string/String/#char_slices"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul String.char_slices()}} method to provide an iterator of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/string/string_slice/StringSlice/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul StringSlice}} instances for each character. 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 StringRef
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  has been removed in favor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/string/string_slice/StringSlice/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul StringSlice}}. And various functionality has moved from 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 String
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 StringLiteral
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  to the more general 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 StringSlice
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  type. See \cf5 \ul Standard library changes\cf2 \ulnone  for more details.\
\ls104\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
You can now use {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/builtin/simd/SIMD/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul SIMD}} constructors to cast existing 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 SIMD
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values (including 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Scalar
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values) to a different type, though you can still use the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/builtin/simd/SIMD/#cast"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul SIMD.cast()}} method to infer the size of the new vector. See \cf5 \ul Standard library changes\cf2 \ulnone  for more details.\
