\f2\fs48 \cf2 \uc0\u10024 
\f0  Highlights\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Here's a brief summary of some of the major changes in this release, with more detailed information in the following sections:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls111\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 inout
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 borrowed
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  argument conventions have been renamed to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mut
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 read
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , respectively. A new 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 out
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  convention has been added for the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 self
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  argument in constructors and for named results. See \cf5 \ul Language changes\cf2 \ulnone  for details.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls111\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Lifetime
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and related types in the standard library have been renamed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/builtin/type_aliases/Origin/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul Origin}} to better clarify that parameters of this type indicate where a reference is derived from, not the more complicated notion of where a variable is initialized and destroyed. As a consequence the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __lifetime_of()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  operator is now named 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __origin_of()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\uc0\u8232 There are also a number of other origin-related improvements in this release, including being able to specify a union of origins by listing multiple values in the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __origin_of()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  operator or inside the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ref
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  origin specifier (
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ref [a, b]
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ). For details, see \cf5 \ul Language changes\cf2 \ulnone .\uc0\u8232 For background information and rationale on the name change see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/modular/modular/issues/3623"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul the proposal}}. For more information on origins, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/values/lifetimes/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul Lifetimes, origins and references}} in the Mojo Manual.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls111\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Implicit conversions are now opt-in using the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/decorators/implicit/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul @implicit}} decorator. See \cf5 \ul Language changes\cf2 \ulnone  for details.\
\ls111\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The standard library has added several new types, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/collections/deque/Deque/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul Deque}} (a double-ended queue) and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/memory/owned_pointer/OwnedPointer/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul OwnedPointer}} (safe, single-owner, non-nullable smart pointer). See \cf5 \ul Standard library changes\cf2 \ulnone  for details.\
\ls111\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The VS Code extension now supports setting data breakpoints and function breakpoints, and the Mojo LLDB debugger supports symbol breakpoints, such as 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 b main
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  or 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 b my_module::main
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\ls111\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
