\fs48 \cf2 Tooling changes\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls115\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The VS Code Mojo Debugger now has a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 buildArgs
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  JSON debug configuration setting that can be used in conjunction with 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojoFile
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  to define the build arguments when compiling the Mojo file.\
\ls115\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The VS Code extension now supports a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Configure Build and Run Args
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  command that helps set the build and run args for actions file 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Run Mojo File
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Debug Mojo File
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . A corresponding button appears in 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Run and Debug
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  selector in the top right corner of a Mojo File.\
\ls115\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The VS Code extension now has the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo.run.focusOnTerminalAfterLaunch
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  setting, which controls whether to focus on the terminal used by the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Mojo: Run Mojo File
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  command or on the editor after launch. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/modular/modular/issues/3532"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul Issue #3532}}.\
\ls115\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The VS Code extension now has the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo.SDK.additionalSDKs
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  setting, which allows the user to provide a list of MAX SDKs that the extension can use when determining a default SDK to use. The user can select the default SDK to use with the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Mojo: Select the default MAX SDK
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  command.\
\ls115\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The VS Code extension now supports setting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/editor/debugging#_data-breakpoints"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul data breakpoints}} as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/editor/debugging#_function-breakpoints"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul function breakpoints}}.\
\ls115\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Mojo LLDB debugger now supports symbol breakpoints, for example, 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 b main
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  or 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 b my_module::main
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\ls115\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Error messages that include type names no longer include inferred or defaulted parameters when they aren't needed. For example, previously Mojo complained about things like:\uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf14 \cb13 ... cannot be converted from 'UnsafePointer[UInt, 0, _default_alignment::AnyType](), MutableAnyOrigin]' to 'UnsafePointer[Int, 0, _default_alignment[::AnyType](), MutableAnyOrigin]'\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls115\ilvl0\cf10 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\uc0\u8232 \cf14 \cb13 \uc0\u8232 
\fs32 \cf16 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cf17 \uc0\u8232 \cf16 \uc0\u8232 \cf14 \uc0\u8232 \cb13 \uc0\u8232 \cf2 \cb1 it now complains more helpfully that:\uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf14 \cb13 ... cannot be converted from 'UnsafePointer[UInt]' to 'UnsafePointer[Int]'\cb1 \
\ls115\ilvl0\cf10 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\uc0\u8232 \cf14 \cb13 \uc0\u8232 
\fs32 \cf16 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cf17 \uc0\u8232 \cf16 \uc0\u8232 \cf14 \uc0\u8232 \cf2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
