Mojo will now link to a Python dynamic library based on the Python on top of your search path: 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 PATH
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . This enables you to activate a virtual environment like 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 conda
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and have access to Python modules installed in that environment without setting 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 MOJO_PYTHON_LIBRARY
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . Previously Mojo would find a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 libpython
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  dynamic library on installation and put the path in 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 .modular/modular.cfg
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , which could result in version conflicts if you activated a virtual environment of a different Python version.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
