\fs48 \cf2 Tooling changes\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls136\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Invoking 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo package my-package -o my-dir
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  on the command line, where 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 my-package
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  is a Mojo package source directory, and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 my-dir
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  is an existing directory, now outputs a Mojo package to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 my-dir/my-package.mojopkg
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . Previously, this had to be spelled out, as in 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 -o my-dir/my-package.mojopkg
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\ls136\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Mojo Language Server now reports a warning when a local variable is unused.\
\ls136\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Several 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  subcommands now support a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --diagnostic-format
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  option that changes the format with which errors, warnings, and other diagnostics are printed. By specifying 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --diagnostic-format json
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  on the command line, errors and other diagnostics will be output in a structured {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jsonlines.org/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul JSON Lines}} format that is easier for machines to parse.\uc0\u8232 The full list of subcommands that support 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --diagnostic-format
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  is as follows: 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo build
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo doc
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo run
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo package
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo test
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . Further, the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo test --json
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  option has been subsumed into this new option; for the same behavior, run 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo test --diagnostic-format json
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\uc0\u8232 Note that the format of the JSON output may change; we don't currently guarantee its stability across releases of Mojo.\
\ls136\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A new 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --validate-doc-strings
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  option has been added to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  to emit errors on invalid doc strings instead of warnings.\
\ls136\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --warn-missing-doc-strings
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  flag for 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  has been renamed to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --diagnose-missing-doc-strings
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\ls136\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A new decorator, 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 @doc_private
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , was added that can be used to hide a declaration from being generated in the output of 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mojo doc
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . It also removes the requirement that the declaration has documentation (for example, when used with 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 --diagnose-missing-doc-strings
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ).\
\ls136\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Debugger users can now set breakpoints on function calls in O0 builds even if the call has been inlined by the compiler.\
\ls136\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Mojo Language Server now supports renaming local variables.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

